# Foundry Environment Configuration

## Required Variables

| Variable | Description | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | SQLite database URL | `sqlite:///data/foundry.db` |
| `SECRET_KEY` | Secret key for session signing | Generated automatically |
| `SESSION_DAYS` | Session duration in days | `30` |
| `COOKIE_SECURE` | Whether cookies are secure (HTTPS only) | `false` (local development) |

## Optional Variables

| Variable | Description | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `AI_ENABLED` | Whether Claude AI drafting is enabled | `false` |
| `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` | Claude model name (if AI enabled) | `claude-3-opus-20240229` |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | Python logging level | `INFO` |

## Usage Example

```bash
# Copy this file and adjust values
cp .env.example .env

# Start the application
python -m app.main
```

## Development

For local development, no environment variables are strictly required.
The application will use sensible defaults for SQLite-based local development.

## Production Notes

- `DATABASE_URL` should point to a persistent location
- `SECRET_KEY` should be a strong random string
- `COOKIE_SECURE` should be `true` when behind HTTPS
- `AI_ENABLED` should remain `false` unless using Claude API with valid credentials